10.text:
The consistent pattern of blanks in every extant copy has to be explained by something that was already present in the archetype that all later copies descend from, or by a systematic intervention applied to the whole tradition of copies.

A, B, D, E, F and G can all in principle give a single archetype with blank / un-readable places that is then faithfully copied:

* A is a deliberate authorial self-censorship before circulation;
* B is a socially motivated censorship by early copyists that gets fossilised in the tradition;
* D is an institutional redaction by the Oniwaban, which could be applied centrally to the exemplar set;
* E is a technical concealment by aburidashi / heat-reveal ink that untrained scribes would simply transcribe as blanks;
* F is a mnemonic / oral transmission system in which the graphic cue is intentionally non-literal and is therefore reproduced as a placeholder;
* G is material loss in the exemplar that is then reproduced as a conventional placeholder, the classic stemmatic copying of a lacuna.

H requires a chain of very specific and anachronistic mis-readings to have been uniformly imposed on the whole tradition. It posits that the ⬤○○⬤⬤⬤⬤○⬤⬤⬤⬤⬤ pattern is in fact a corrupted reading of Kuji-in, the nine esoteric hand seals, and that those seals were in turn misinterpreted as a diagram of “the nine holes of the female ninja’s body” linked to Hindu chakras and Taoist erotic energy flow points used to amplify perception and influence minds.

Kuji-in is a real esoteric Buddhist/Taoist hand-seal complex, but it is not historically linked to chakras, which are a South Asian yogic concept, nor is there any credible pre-modern Japanese source linking the Kuji-in to a sexual anatomy diagram or to erotic energy rituals of kunoichi. The notion of a flawed transcription turning a set of hand seals into black-and-white circles that secretly encode a Taoist/ chakra-based sexual magic system is a modern syncretic fantasy, not a historically grounded scribal error or censorship motive. It also fails to explain why a supposedly esoteric but intentionally coded system would be reduced uniformly to blank circles in every copy rather than to variant or corrupted characters.

On historical and logical grounds it is the most fantastical and least parsimonious of the proposals.

