3.text:
The diagnostic is the identical ⬤○○⬤⬤⬤⬤○⬤⬤⬤⬤⬤ placeholder in every extant witness. That is a stemmatic, archetype-level absence, not independent per-copy accidents.

A, B, D, E and F all give a single point of systematic blanking that will then be faithfully copied:
* authorial / social / institutional redaction, A/B/D;
* technical concealment, E aburidashi invisible ink which a non-initiate scribe would copy as blank;
* a mnemonic / oral cue system, F, misread as a literal placeholder.

G is debatable on identicality but remains codicologically possible: a heavily consulted passage in the exemplar that fed the whole tradition fades/wears first, the first copyist marks the illegible positions with a conventional lacuna siglum — the black/white circles — and the siglum is then inherited. The identicality is the problem for G, not the physical loss per se.

C is conspiratorial and historically unsupported — Lady Saigō as stepdaughter of Hattori, a kunoichi-backed Tokugawa legitimacy cover-up, etc. — but it stays inside a political/institutional censorship logic.

H is the only option that cannot be accommodated by documented Edo-period manuscript, ninjutsu or esoteric practice. It requires:

* Kuji-in/Kujiho, a Shingon/Onmyōdō nine-seal system, to be conflated with Hindu chakras and Taoist erotic energy rituals, a modern New Age syncretism with no pre-modern Japanese attestation;
* a “nine holes of the female ninja’s body” anatomical/energetic mapping and a yin-yang erotic mind-influence rite that never appears in Bansenshukai scholarship;
* a “flawed transcription” that turns esoteric hand seals into a fixed 13-position black/white circle string. The claimed nine-seal origin does not even match the data — the pattern is 13 positions, not nine — and there is no textual, iconographic or codicological evidence that transcribers ever systematically reduced such a diagram to uniform placeholders.

The other hypotheses are at least grounded in known scribal practice, censorship, secrecy or material loss. H is anachronistic pseudohistory imposed on the lacuna. It is the least plausible explanation of the set.

2.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: H

The ⬤○○⬤⬤⬤⬤○⬤⬤⬤⬤⬤ string is identical in every extant witness. That is a stemmatic fact. It is not independent fading in independent copies, it is a single archetypal state that is being faithfully reproduced downstream.

A, B, D, E, F and even G can all generate a single archetypal blank that is then copied:

* A self-censorship by Fujibayashi before presentation;
* B a Tokugawa neo-Confucian modesty taboo that fossilises in the tradition;
* D Oniwaban institutional redaction for state secrecy;
* E aburidashi heat-reveal ink that a non-initiate copyist would transcribe as blank;
* F a schematic mnemonic / colour cue for oral transmission that is reproduced literally by literate but non-initiate scribes;
* G material loss in the exemplar that fed the whole tradition, with the lacuna marked by a conventional placeholder and then copied.

All of those are grounded in Edo-period manuscript control, ninja tradecraft and scribal practice.

H is not grounded at all. It requires Kuji-in/Kujiho, a Shingon/Onmyōdō nine-seal system, to be conflated with Hindu chakras and with a Taoist erotic “nine holes of the female ninja’s body” diagram used for perception and mind-influence rituals. There is no pre-modern Japanese source linking Kuji-in to chakras, to sexual alchemy, or to female anatomy mapping, and no Bansenshukai witness supports an erotic-mystical reading of the Kunoichi no Jutsu. The claim is modern New-Age / pop-occult syncretism projected backwards.

The material claim also fails. The emblem in the problem is 13 positions, ⬤○○⬤⬤⬤⬤○⬤⬤⬤⬤⬤, not nine, so it cannot be a “nine holes / Kujiho” derivation even on its own terms. A genuine misreading of esoteric seals would produce variation between copyists and marginal glosses attempting to make sense of them, not the same regularised black/white circle placeholder in every lineage.

C and G are speculative, but they stay inside the logic of censorship, conspiracy and codicology. H is a pseudohistorical mash-up with no textual, iconographic or historiographic lineage, making it the least plausible explanation for a stable, patterned lacuna.

